From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:35:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the IoT Jobs ID length when resuming a bootstrap
 deployment

retrieve_in_progress_deployment() copies the saved jobs ID into the
caller's 64-byte buffer but leaves the buffer's length at 64. The resumed
deployment then reports its status for a job ID padded with NUL bytes,
which AWS IoT Jobs rejects as InvalidRequest; the rejection is treated as
permanent, so the job stays IN_PROGRESS and the cloud deployment never
completes. Every cloud deployment with a bootstrap step (which always
reboots the device) ends this way.

Set the length to that of the saved ID.

Signed-off-by: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Upstream: not yet submitted; also present on upstream main (8552acf)
---
 modules/ggdeploymentd/src/bootstrap_manager.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/modules/ggdeploymentd/src/bootstrap_manager.c b/modules/ggdeploymentd/src/bootstrap_manager.c
index ae4a430..1c612dc 100644
--- a/modules/ggdeploymentd/src/bootstrap_manager.c
+++ b/modules/ggdeploymentd/src/bootstrap_manager.c
@@ -268,6 +268,7 @@ GgError retrieve_in_progress_deployment(
         gg_obj_into_buf(*jobs_id_obj).data,
         gg_obj_into_buf(*jobs_id_obj).len
     );
+    jobs_id->len = gg_obj_into_buf(*jobs_id_obj).len;
 
     GgObject *deployment_type;
     ret = gg_map_validate(
